WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:03.469
-It's time for
"Tonight Show Hashtags"!

00:00:03.469 --> 00:00:08.074
-♪ Hashtags ♪

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:09.442
♪ Hashtags ♪

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:12.911
♪♪

00:00:12.911 --> 00:00:18.217
-Hey, we do this thing
where I send out a -- hey! --

00:00:18.217 --> 00:00:20.553
hashtag, and we ask you guys
to respond to that topic.

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:22.622
So, for this week,
I asked you guys to describe

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:24.257
your summer --
best describe your summer

00:00:24.257 --> 00:00:27.293 line:0%
using the hashtag
"MySummerInSixWords."

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:29.662 line:0%
For example,
I sent out a tweet that said,

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:31.664 line:0%
"Feel the heat,
smell the breath."

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:33.133
Within minutes,
the hashtag became

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:35.668
the number-one trending topic
in the U.S.,

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:37.069
so thank you for playing along.

00:00:37.069 --> 00:00:39.072
We want to do this
every week here.

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:40.873
So, now I thought I'd share
some of my favorite

00:00:40.873 --> 00:00:44.144
"MySummerInSixWords"
responses from you guys.

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:48.714
This first one here
is from @Lopey Wopey.

00:00:48.714 --> 00:00:52.251
She says, "Didn't know noses
sweat, until now."

00:00:52.251 --> 00:00:55.321
They do. And chins, too.

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:58.324
This one is from @taylorlynea.

00:00:58.324 --> 00:01:03.796
She says,
"Trash goes out more than me."

00:01:03.796 --> 00:01:05.731
That's smart. Keeping it safe.

00:01:05.731 --> 00:01:08.001
This one's from
@melodybutler.

00:01:08.001 --> 00:01:13.806
She says, "'The best summer
ever,' says my dog."

00:01:13.806 --> 00:01:18.477
This one is
from @vansha2017.

00:01:18.477 --> 00:01:22.582
They say, "Let's hang!
Sending you the link."

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:25.018
That sums up the summer.
-Yeah.

00:01:25.018 --> 00:01:26.552
"Let's hang!
I'll send you the link."

00:01:26.552 --> 00:01:28.988
Yeah. We're all gonna log on
at 7:00.

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:34.760
This one is from @CapnOMySoul.

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:37.563
That's kind of romantic,
Kind of?

00:01:37.563 --> 00:01:39.698
Well, if it was "captain,"
it would probably be more.

00:01:39.698 --> 00:01:41.300
"Capn" makes it feel
like a cereal.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:44.604
-You got to say it fast
like Kirk's name -- "Capn."

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:47.573
"Captain of my soul"?
-No, just the "capn" part.

00:01:47.573 --> 00:01:48.908
-Oh.
-CapnOMySoul.

00:01:48.908 --> 00:01:50.777
-Oh, CapnOMySoul.
-Yeah.

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:52.045
-Yeah. But it's like Cap'n.

00:01:52.045 --> 00:01:53.579
It's kind of spelled
like the cereal.

00:01:53.579 --> 00:01:55.448
-Yeah, Cap'n Crunch,
Captain Kirk.

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:58.351
-Takes me out a little bit.
Well, it's Cap'n Kirk?

00:01:58.351 --> 00:02:00.586
-It's Cap'n. Cap'n.
-It's not Captain?

00:02:00.586 --> 00:02:03.956
-No.
-It's Cap'n, like the cereal.

00:02:03.956 --> 00:02:05.390
-You look disappointed.
-Yeah.

00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:06.625
-Yeah, I'm bummed out.

00:02:06.625 --> 00:02:09.862
-It's been 12 years.

00:02:09.862 --> 00:02:12.164
-I don't call him "Captain."
Come on.

00:02:12.164 --> 00:02:14.934
That would be weird.

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:16.969
Hey, Captain. I guess it is.

00:02:16.969 --> 00:02:18.905
Anyways, CapnOMy-- Sorry.

00:02:18.905 --> 00:02:20.773
CapnOMySoul -- he says,

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:23.976
"Yes, Netflix. Still watching.
Always watching."

00:02:23.976 --> 00:02:26.279
Stop asking me.

00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:30.083
This next one is from
@Klean Killer.

00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:32.518
-Ooh.

00:02:32.518 --> 00:02:38.825
He says, "Tell us about
outside again, Daddy."

00:02:38.825 --> 00:02:41.227
This one is from
@MelissaBuntcake.

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:42.961
Think that's her real last name?

00:02:42.961 --> 00:02:45.298
-Buntcake?
-Yeah. Melissa Buntcake?

00:02:45.298 --> 00:02:48.434
-Yeah, it's probably
pronounced differently.

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:50.536
-Buntkik?

00:02:50.536 --> 00:02:54.273
-Buntkake.
-Hey, hey! Hey!

00:02:54.273 --> 00:02:56.309
-Come on, man.

00:02:56.309 --> 00:02:57.743
-Oh, yeah. Maybe, yeah.

00:02:57.743 --> 00:03:00.846
I didn't see the
line over the "E." Alright.

00:03:00.846 --> 00:03:04.483
She says, "Melissa,
can you mute your mic?"

00:03:04.483 --> 00:03:05.885
That's pretty good.

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:13.026
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.026 --> 00:03:16.396
This one is from @catmomto8.

00:03:16.396 --> 00:03:18.831
She says, "Didn't we already
watch this episode?"

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:20.767
I know, but watch --
It's "Ozark."

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:24.204
Come on, man.
Every episode is good.

00:03:24.204 --> 00:03:25.204
Have you seen that, by the way?
"Ozark"?

00:03:25.204 --> 00:03:26.505
-Yes.
-Yep.

00:03:26.505 --> 00:03:28.408
-I'm only on Episode 3.

00:03:28.408 --> 00:03:30.310
-Of the most recent season
or period?

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:31.877
-No. Season 1.
-Oh, wow.

00:03:31.877 --> 00:03:33.378
-Oh, wow.
-Yeah.

00:03:33.378 --> 00:03:34.480
-You're going to have fun.
-Really?

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:35.615
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:03:35.615 --> 00:03:37.016
I love it.
I love every second of it.

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:38.151
-Yeah, it's crazy.

00:03:38.151 --> 00:03:40.119
-And everyone's, like,
a good character.

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:42.421
Everyone's -- Oh.
-Bateman's the man, you know?

00:03:42.421 --> 00:03:44.056
-He's crushin' it,
Jason Bateman.

00:03:44.056 --> 00:03:45.191
-Yep.
-Yeah, man.

00:03:45.191 --> 00:03:48.127
This last one is from
@SeaWolf510.

00:03:48.127 --> 00:03:51.230
He says, "Can someone please
yell 'Jumanji' already?"

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:53.165
Yeah, perfect.
There you have it.

00:03:53.165 --> 00:03:55.034
Those are our
"Tonight Show Hashtags."

